<title>FRANCE: FRENCH ELECTION - OPINION POLL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>FRENCH ELECTION - OPINION POLL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the results of opinion polls</p>
<p>conducted since President Jacques Chirac dissolved the National Assembly on</p>
<p>April 21 and called a snap election for May 25 and June 1.</p>
<p>No polls have been published since Saturday, the last day results could be</p>
<p>released in France ahead of the election.</p>
<p>The dates indicate when the poll was taken. The first table is of voting</p>
<p>intentions in percentage terms. Most surveys have a margin of error of plus or</p>
<p>minus two percent.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>			 Extreme  Communist Socialist Ecologist  RPR/UDF    Nat</p>
<p>			  left		   + allies		+ allies  Front</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Sofres   16-17/5    2	   10	  28	   6	  40	  13</p>
<p> IFOP     16/5	 2.5	 10	  27	   6.5	39.5	14</p>
<p> CSA	16-17/5    3.5	 10.5	26.5	 8	  37.5	14</p>
<p> BVA	15-16/5    2	   10.5	27	   7	  38.5	14</p>
<p> L.Harris 15-16/5    2.5	  9.5	27	   7	  39	  15</p>
<p> CSA	15-16/5    3	   10.5	27	   7.5	38	  14</p>
<p> Ipsos    13-14/5    1.5	  9	  28.5	 5.5	39	  15</p>
<p> L.Harris 12-13/5    2	   10	  29	   7	  37.5	14.5</p>
<p> CSA	12-13/5    1.5	 10.5	28	   7	  39.5	13.5</p>
<p> BVA	 9-10/5    1.5	 11.5	27	   8	  37.5	14.5</p>
<p> L.Harris  9-10/5    2	    9	  28	   6	  40	  15</p>
<p> Sofres    9-10/5    2	   10	  29.5	 5	  39.5	14</p>
<p> IFOP	  9/5     3	    9	  26.5	 7	  41	  13.5</p>
